## PART 7: BEST PRACTICES COMPLIANCE

### 7.1 Cursor IDE Best Practices

**Rule File Structure**: Single source of truth (`MASTER-RULES-PART1.mdc` and `MASTER-RULES-PART2.mdc`), proper YAML frontmatter, clear organization (2 parts, both under 500 lines), no conflicts, actionable rules with examples.

### 7.2 Git Workflow Best Practices

**PR-Centric Workflow**: One active PR per agent targeting `beta`, PR branches exist only while PR is open, all work flows through PR, sequential PR merging, automatic cleanup keeps only `main` and `beta`.

**Pre-commit Hooks**: CMake flag validator, AI-assisted review (optional), hooks run automatically, **AUTOMATIC** auto-fix and re-run on failure, **NO USER INTERVENTION**.

**CI/CD Integration**: GitHub Actions workflow, 7 automated validation checks on PR/push, comprehensive coverage.

### 7.3 Automation Best Practices

**Maximum Automation**: Auto-fix all errors, auto-resolve conflicts, auto-merge when clean, auto-cleanup, auto-classify commits.

**User Intervention ONLY When**: Multiple solution options exist with different pros/cons, or **RARE** auto-resolution failure with multiple valid strategies.

**AUTOMATIC HANDLING**: All validation errors → Auto-fixed, all critical issues → Auto-resolved, all merges → Performed automatically, all fixes → Batched → Single commit → Single push, **BATCHING CRITICAL** for clean build tree.

### 7.4 User Communication Best Practices

**Feedback Level**: Immediate status updates, adequate detail (not overwhelming), clear error messages, summary format "Action → Result → Next Step", avoid atomic-level details, always include repository name and path.

### 7.5 Build Tree Cleanliness

**Branch Management**: Only `main` and `beta` remain after cleanup, PR branches deleted immediately, PRs closed immediately, no orphaned branches.

**File Management**: Only core files modified, no temporary files, no patch scripts, no workflow files.

**Commit/Push Management**: **BATCH ALL FIXES** → **SINGLE COMMIT** → **SINGLE PUSH** → Clean history, minimal pushes.

### 7.6 Early Error Detection

**Multi-Layer Validation**: Pre-commit hooks (early), post-push agent validation (thorough), CI/CD checks (continuous). Auto-fix capabilities, comprehensive checklists, multiple validation stages, clear error messages.

### 7.7 Context Management

- ✅ Keep every prompt/checklist/rule reference under Cursor's context limit (≤500 lines per file)
- ✅ Chunk large instructions into targeted references
- ✅ Summarize long outputs before re-posting
- ✅ Trim optional flags/comments for concise content
- ✅ Monitor conversation length; move artifacts to rule files (within size limits)
- ✅ Both PART1 and PART2 must remain under 500 lines each

